00:46:40,000 --> 00:46:46,000
Strange Darling is a 2023 American psychological crime
thriller film written and directed by JT Mollner.

11
00:51:20,000 --> 00:51:26,000
The film stars Willa Fitzgerald, Kyle Gallner, Madisen Beaty, Steven
Michael Quezada, Ed Begley Jr., and Barbara Hershey.

12
00:56:00,000 --> 00:56:06,000
Set in rural Oregon, it follows a man (Gallner) and woman (Fitzgerald) who have a
one-night stand that devolves into a cat-and-mouse game of murder.

13
01:00:40,000 --> 01:00:46,000
It is divided into six chapters in nonlinear order.

14
01:05:20,000 --> 01:05:26,000
Principal photography began in Portland, Oregon on
August 22, 2022, and concluded on October 1.

15
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
The film marked the cinematographic debut of Giovanni Ribisi, who also
served as one of the producers, and was shot on 35 mm film.

16
01:14:40,000 --> 01:14:46,000
Strange Darling premiered at Fantastic Fest on September 22, 2023, and was
theatrically released in the United States on August 23, 2024.

17
01:19:20,000 --> 01:19:26,000
The film received positive reviews from critics, with particular praise
for the cinematography and the performances of the cast.

18
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
Despite this, it was a box office failure, grossing $4.8
million against its $4–10 million production budget.

19
01:28:40,000 --> 01:28:46,000
The film explores themes of new york city, rape,
gore, sadomasochism, sexual violence.

20
01:33:20,000 --> 01:33:26,000
The tone is intense and dark and mind_bending.
